& [SJS]
  + Situation: compact requests are reconstructable against retained history but a received or queued packet has no small independent corruption check
  + Justification: a domain-separated request and frame digest makes packet identity inspectable before the host pays the cost of canonical replay validation
  + Solution: wrap each projected transport in a strict self-digested envelope then retain a separate stronger validator against the canonical Slice6C projection

& [Delineation]
  + local integrity asks whether the carried bytes still match their carried digests and shape
  + canonical binding asks whether the entire envelope is the uniquely reconstructed envelope for one validated canonical transport
  + local integrity cannot establish provenance authenticity host custody semantic truth model interpretation or provider execution
  + a digest is a corruption-evident identifier and not a keyed signature

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + digest input is domain tag followed by one zero byte followed by deterministic compact JSON bytes
  + all digest algorithms are exactly sha256 with lowercase hexadecimal values
  + phase kind index and optional-field shape are validated independently of hash agreement
  + full-prefix iteration compact iteration and compact terminal envelopes form three explicit structural cases

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty names self-consistency canonical binding and authentication as different claims
  + Security domain-separates frame and request digests and refuses malformed optional-field combinations
  + Planner fixes envelope order and phase-index rules
  + Weaver echoes the retained-prefix digest only where a reentry frame exists
  + Scribe preserves request frame digest and nonclaim evidence in strict normalized JSON
  + Refiner supplies the smallest local integrity surface without copying canonical history
  + Observer requires both local and canonical validation in fixture acceptance

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated transport_envelope forms compilation validation projection normalization and adversarial tests
  + keep signatures key trust provider execution and persistence under separate future authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove without changing predecessor forms or behavior
